-    /// A FRESH program over the same workspace, `path`'s own text
-    /// overridden to `text` — every other file read exactly as the
-    /// original's host reads it, and `entry` its entry file: a script's
-    /// own statements are judged only under the entry. Never written to disk: the proof is
