-
-    /// A FRESH program whose ONLY ENTRY is `path`, its text overridden to `text`: every
-    /// top-level statement of every file below its own offset is silenced — `path`'s
-    /// below `kept_from`, any other file's all — so what runs is the statements `text`
-    /// carries from `kept_from` on. Declarations stay where they stand and stay in scope.
-    /// Never written to disk.
-    fn entered_over(path: string, text: string, kept_from: int) -> Program {
